&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mixpanel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mixpanel is the leading product intelligence and analytics platform, trusted by more than 29,000 companies to help understand how people use the products they build. By combining powerful analytics with AI that knows your business, Mixpanel helps teams see what’s working, diagnose what’s not, and decide what to build next. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://mixpanel.com/home/&quot;&gt;mixpanel.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mixpanel&#39;s Legal team is small, commercial and global, supporting the business globally on commercial contracting, privacy, marketing, partnerships and procurement. We run lean, so you will own matters end to end and work directly with the business rather than at arm&#39;s length. We treat legal as a revenue enabler and invest heavily in playbooks, tooling and AI so a small team can cover a lot of ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The role requires a licensed Singapore-based attorney who is motivated, diligent, collaborative, business-minded, and has a wide breadth of experience drafting, negotiating, and collaborating with internal teams to support both inbound and outbound commercial transactions. This individual has exceptional written and verbal communication skills, has a critical eye for identifying and resolving issues and concerns by proactively collaborating with other legal team members and internal stakeholders across the organization, and will help develop legal resources, contract templates, and documentation to inform and facilitate contracting efforts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and negotiate technology-related commercial agreements with the Company’s customers, including master services and SaaS agreements, data processing addenda , data security addenda, and NDAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, negotiate, and structure vendor and partnership agreements, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and iterate on the legal team’s AI initiatives, policies, processes and procedures to improve the legal team’s engagement model across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide pragmatic legal and strategic support on cross-functional projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise cross-functional teams on meeting strategic objectives while complying with global laws, regulations, best practices, and customer requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product, engineering, security, and other business units to ensure privacy by design principles are embedded in Mixpanel products, services and business arrangements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re Looking For Someone Who:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 5+ years of experience drafting and negotiating inbound and outbound commercial agreements, including SaaS agreements, with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating data protection agreements and advising on data privacy questions and concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with product and regulatory counseling related to healthcare, financial services, consumer protection, and data security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive, friendly and collaborative attitude while maintaining the highest standards of business and professional conduct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills with the ability to respond to requests quickly and with excellent attention to detail in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication skills, both verbal and written, and a demonstrated ability to establish and maintain collaborative working relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker with a focus on practical solutions that are geared towards reducing company risk while being fair and balanced.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work flexibly and efficiently, prioritize work and meet demanding deadlines in a fast-paced environment, especially during quarter-end.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points for experience or an interest in:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiating enterprise deals with enterprise customers in key APAC geographies such as Singapore, India and Indonesia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Local entity administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting with local employment-related matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#PC-LI&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive Medical, Vision, and Dental Care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Wellness Benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Vacation Policy &amp;amp; Additional Company Holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer Time Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional US Benefits: Pre-Tax Benefits including 401(K), Wellness Benefit, Holiday Break&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*please note that benefits and perks for contract positions will vary*&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make Bold Bets:&lt;/strong&gt; We choose courageous action over comfortable progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovate with Insight:&lt;/strong&gt; We tackle decisions with rigor and judgment - combining data, experience and collective wisdom to drive&amp;nbsp;powerful outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One Team:&lt;/strong&gt; We collaborate across boundaries to achieve far greater impact than any of us could accomplish alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candor with Connection:&lt;/strong&gt; We build meaningful relationships that enable honest feedback and direct conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion the Customer:&lt;/strong&gt; We seek to deeply understand our customers’ needs, ensuring their success is our north star.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Powerful Simplicity:&lt;/strong&gt; We find elegant solutions to complex problems, making sophisticated things accessible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why choose Mixpanel?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a leader in analytics with over 29,000 customers and $277M invested from prominent investors: like Andreessen-Horowitz, Sequoia, YC, and, most recently, Bain Capital. Mixpanel’s pioneering event-based data analytics platform offers a powerful yet simple solution for companies to understand user behaviors and easily track overarching company success metrics. Our accomplished teams continuously facilitate our expansion by tackling the ever-evolving challenges tied to scaling, reliability, design, and service. Choosing to work at Mixpanel means you’ll be helping the world’s most innovative companies learn from their data so they can make better decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mixpanel is an equal opportunity employer supporting workforce diversity. At Mixpanel, we are focused on things that really matter—our people, our customers, our partners—out of a recognition that those relationships are the most valuable assets we have. We actively encourage women, people with disabilities, veterans, underrepresented minorities, and LGBTQ+ people to apply. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance or other similar laws that may be applicable, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records. We’ve immersed ourselves in our Culture and Values as our guiding principles for the impact we want to have and the future we are building.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mixpanel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mixpanel is the leading product intelligence and analytics platform, trusted by more than 29,000 companies to help understand how people use the products they build. By combining powerful analytics with AI that knows your business, Mixpanel helps teams see what’s working, diagnose what’s not, and decide what to build next. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://mixpanel.com/home/&quot;&gt;mixpanel.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mixpanel&#39;s Customer Engineering team is a cross-functional group of highly technical problem solvers focused on driving customer outcomes across the full commercial lifecycle. Customer Engineers are the technical face of Mixpanel in the field — connecting prospect business problems to Mixpanel&#39;s technical capabilities, running sharp evaluations, and ensuring every customer who signs has a clear, fast path to value. The team works in close partnership with Account Executives on new business and expansion, and hands off to Delivery Engineers to own technical activation post-sale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Customer Engineer owns the pre-sales technical journey — from discovery and technical fit assessment through competitive positioning, demo, and POC. You establish whether Mixpanel is the right technical fit before committing to a proof of concept, and when you do run one, you design it to be immediately actionable by the Delivery Engineer: focus metric defined, data validated, success criteria agreed upon. You also return post-sale for cross-sell and strategic expansion that requires a new technical evaluation. A great CE shows up researched, thinks in outcomes, leaves every interaction with more clarity than they walked in with, and treats handoff quality as a first-class output.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical discovery, establishing the prospect&#39;s business challenges, technical environment, and qualification before committing to a POC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver tailored, research-backed demos that connect Mixpanel&#39;s capabilities to the prospect&#39;s specific business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish technical fit — confirm the prospect&#39;s stack is a match and scope what a meaningful proof requires before the POC begins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own competitive technical positioning — be the definitive answer to why Mixpanel over Amplitude, PostHog, and warehouse-native alternatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run tightly structured POCs with defined success criteria, a named focus metric, and a handoff package the Delivery Engineer can execute from immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Return post-sale for cross-sell and strategic expansion requiring a new technical evaluation on a new surface or product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Executives on deal strategy, technical objection handling, and expansion planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to Delivery Engineers to understand production realities — your POCs should reflect what actually works in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re Looking For Someone Who Has&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–4+ years of experience in Solutions Engineering, Sales Engineering, or a technical pre-sales role at a B2B SaaS company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical foundation in data analytics, event tracking, APIs, data warehouses, or adjacent domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial instinct — you understand that your job is to win deals and you orient your work accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to run structured POCs with defined success criteria and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, compelling communication to technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive knowledge of the analytics landscape, or the ability to build it quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Humble, hungry, smart, and accountable — these are the bar, not aspirations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-value=&quot;{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;The total target compensation (TTC) for this full-time position is $174,600 - $213,400 across the United States. This amount includes base compensation and variable compensation in the form of either a company bonus or commissions. Variable compensation type is determined by your role and level. This position is also eligible for equity consideration and other benefits including medical, vision, and dental insurance coverage. You can view our benefits offerings here.\n\nOur salary ranges are determined by role and level and are benchmarked to the SF Bay Area Technology data cut released by Radford, a global compensation database. The range displayed represents the minimum and maximum TTC for new hire salaries for the position across all of our US locations. To stay on top of market conditions, we refresh our salary ranges twice a year so these ranges may change in the future. Within the range, individual pay is determined by experience, job-related skills, qualifications, and other factors. If you have questions about the specific range, your recruiter can share this information.&amp;quot;}&quot; data-sheets-userformat=&quot;{&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:769,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0},&amp;quot;11&amp;quot;:4,&amp;quot;12&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;The amount listed below is the total target cash compensation (TTCC) and includes base compensation and variable compensation in the form of either a company bonus or commissions. Variable compensation type is determined by your role and level. In addition to the cash compensation provided, this position is also eligible for equity consideration and other benefits including medical, vision, and dental insurance coverage. You can view our benefits offerings &lt;a href=&quot;https://mxpnl.notion.site/Check-out-our-benefits-869112a6cabe4c81a2b9da99de28f636&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our salary ranges are determined by role and level and are benchmarked to the SF Bay Area Technology data cut released by Radford, a global compensation database. The range displayed represents the minimum and maximum TTCC for new hire salaries for the position across all of our US locations. To stay on top of market conditions, we refresh our salary ranges twice a year so these ranges may change in the future. Within the range, individual pay is determined by experience, job-related skills, qualifications, and other factors. If you have questions about the specific range, your recruiter can share this information.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Mixpanel Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$132,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$179,500 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive Medical, Vision, and Dental Care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Wellness Benefit&lt;/li&gt;
